Reused evidence
- None.

New evidence
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"The 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia, Indonesia","publisher":"WIPO Lex","publication_date":"best available","url":"https://www.wipo.int/wipolex/en/legislation/details/7987","claim":"The president serves a five-year term with only one reelection, is supreme commander of the armed forces, may declare war/make peace and conclude treaties with DPR approval, appoints and dismisses ministers, and can be removed only through the constitutional impeachment process.","locator":"Articles 7, 10-11, 17, 7A-7B","source_type":"primary/legal","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official constitutional text on an authoritative legal database; stable and directly governing 2022 office powers.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Standing constitutional framework in force throughout 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Office-level authority and constraints for Jokowi as president; not a performance claim.","contrary_evidence":["No nuclear-specific authority appears in the text; it defines general executive powers, not nuclear command.","Several core powers are constrained by DPR and judicial procedures."],"lenses":["1B.3","1B.4","1B.7","1B.8"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Soal Presiden Tiga Periode, Presiden Jokowi: Kita Harus Taat Konstitusi","publisher":"Sekretariat Kabinet Republik Indonesia","publication_date":"2022-03-30","url":"https://setkab.go.id/soal-presiden-tiga-periode-presiden-jokowi-kita-harus-taat-konstitusi/","claim":"Jokowi said the constitution already regulates presidential terms and that everyone must obey it, in response to three-term talk.","locator":"paras. 46-49","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct presidential statement published by the Cabinet Secretariat on the same day.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 ruler statement during the term-extension controversy.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Jokowi statement.","contrary_evidence":["Self-reporting is not independent verification of broader coalition behavior.","It rejects three-term talk but does not by itself show long-term institutional restraint."],"lenses":["1B.1","1B.10"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Introductory Remarks of President of the Republic of Indonesia at Limited Cabinet Meeting on the Preparation for the 2024 Simultaneous General Elections and Regional Elections","publisher":"Sekretariat Kabinet Republik Indonesia","publication_date":"2022-04-10","url":"https://setkab.go.id/en/introductory-remarks-of-president-of-the-republic-of-indonesia-at-limited-cabinet-meeting-on-the-preparation-for-the-2024-simultaneous-general-elections-and-regional-elections-bogor-presidential-pala/","claim":"Jokowi said the 2024 election schedule was already fixed and that the government should prevent speculation about postponing the election or extending the president’s term.","locator":"paras. 41-43","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct presidential remarks published by the Cabinet Secretariat with explicit dates and policy context.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 statement during the term-extension debate.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Jokowi statement.","contrary_evidence":["This addresses constitutional timing, not nuclear or existential-risk policy.","It shows rejection of postponement speculation, not a broader institutional reform program."],"lenses":["1B.1","1B.10"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Presiden Jokowi Instruksikan Jajaran Antisipasi Krisis Pangan dan Energi","publisher":"Sekretariat Kabinet Republik Indonesia","publication_date":"2022-06-20","url":"https://setkab.go.id/presiden-jokowi-instruksikan-jajaran-antisipasi-krisis-pangan-dan-energi/","claim":"Jokowi instructed officials to anticipate global food and energy crises, manage subsidies and inefficiencies, and keep domestic prices stable during global uncertainty.","locator":"paras. 45-55","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct government transcript of Jokowi’s cabinet instructions with dated context and concrete policy guidance.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Direct 2022 crisis-management speech.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Jokowi statement.","contrary_evidence":["This is broad economic crisis management, not a nuclear-risk decision.","It supports end-posture context more than any nuclear-specific lens."],"lenses":["1B.10"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"War in Ukraine Must be Stopped: President Jokowi","publisher":"Sekretariat Kabinet Republik Indonesia","publication_date":"2022-05-14","url":"https://setkab.go.id/en/war-in-ukraine-must-be-stopped-president-jokowi/","claim":"Jokowi called for ending the war in Ukraine immediately and said war benefits nobody; leaders bear responsibility to create conditions for peace.","locator":"paras. 38-40","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct presidential remarks published by the Cabinet Secretariat shortly after the summit appearance.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 crisis-de-escalation statement during the Ukraine war.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Jokowi statement.","contrary_evidence":["Not nuclear-specific, so it is only indirect evidence for 1B.2/1B.8.","It is a generic antiwar statement, not a command or treaty action."],"lenses":["1B.1","1B.2","1B.8"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Treaty on the Non-Proliferation of Nuclear Weapons","publisher":"United Nations Office for Disarmament Affairs","publication_date":"best available","url":"https://disarmament.unoda.org/en/our-work/weapons-mass-destruction/nuclear-weapons/treaty-non-proliferation-nuclear-weapons","claim":"The NPT aims to prevent the spread of nuclear weapons, promote peaceful uses of nuclear energy, and further nuclear disarmament; it also establishes IAEA safeguards to verify compliance.","locator":"paras. 389-393","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official UNODA treaty explainer with clear summary of the treaty’s purpose and verification architecture.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Standing treaty framework applicable in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Country-level treaty posture, not a Jokowi-only action.","contrary_evidence":["This is treaty architecture, not proof of a specific 2022 presidential choice.","It explains constraints and posture rather than personal conduct."],"lenses":["1B.4","1B.9"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Country List: Indonesia, Republic of","publisher":"IAEA Office of Legal Affairs","publication_date":"best available","url":"https://ola.iaea.org/Applications/FactSheets/Country/Detail?code=ID","claim":"Indonesia has a comprehensive safeguards agreement and an additional protocol in force with the IAEA, along with CPPNM and other nuclear-safety treaties.","locator":"Safeguards Agreements and Agreements sections, lines 111-123 and 34-42","source_type":"primary/legal","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official IAEA country treaty record; directly lists Indonesia’s safeguards and physical-protection commitments.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Standing safeguards status in force during 2022.","ruler_attribution":"State-level nuclear governance; not a direct presidential operational decision.","contrary_evidence":["This shows peaceful-use verification and security commitments, not a warhead or command-and-control decision.","It is evidence of limited exposure and regulatory constraint rather than nuclear agency."],"lenses":["1B.3","1B.9"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Comprehensive Nuclear-Test-Ban Treaty","publisher":"United Nations Office for Disarmament Affairs","publication_date":"best available","url":"https://disarmament.unoda.org/en/our-work/weapons-mass-destruction/nuclear-weapons/comprehensive-nuclear-test-ban-treaty","claim":"Indonesia is listed among the Annex-2 states that have ratified the CTBT.","locator":"Status of the Treaty section","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official UNODA treaty-status page with explicit ratification status for Annex-2 states.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Standing treaty status applicable in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"State treaty posture, not a direct Jokowi-only act in 2022.","contrary_evidence":["Ratification predates 2022 and does not itself show active 2022 leadership.","It is treaty context rather than a ruler-specific crisis choice."],"lenses":["1B.4"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"ASEAN Legal Instruments: Treaty on Southeast Asia Nuclear Weapon-Free Zone","publisher":"ASEAN Secretariat","publication_date":"best available","url":"https://agreement.asean.org/agreement/detail/92.html","claim":"Indonesia ratified the Southeast Asia Nuclear Weapon-Free Zone treaty on 29 November 2011.","locator":"Instruments of Ratification table","source_type":"primary/legal","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official ASEAN legal-instrument database recording member-state ratification dates.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Preexisting regional nonproliferation commitment that remained in force in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"State posture inherited by Jokowi; not a 2022 personal action.","contrary_evidence":["This is long-running regional treaty commitment, not evidence of a 2022 decision by Jokowi.","It constrains posture but does not by itself show active presidential disarmament work."],"lenses":["1B.4"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Preparation of Standard Operating Procedure for Physical Protection October 25, 2022","publisher":"BAPETEN","publication_date":"2022-10-25","url":"https://www.bapeten.go.id/berita/preparation-of-standard-operating-procedure-for-physical-protection-october-25-2022-151958","claim":"BAPETEN said its task is to ensure nuclear use is only for peaceful purposes and to protect nuclear materials and installations; in 2022 it developed inspection procedures for planned and built SMR and MSR facilities.","locator":"paras. 82-87, 91-94","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official regulator statement dated in 2022, with concrete nuclear-security and inspection content.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 nuclear-security governance evidence.","ruler_attribution":"State regulatory system under Jokowi’s government; not a weapon-command decision.","contrary_evidence":["This concerns civilian nuclear safety/security, not weapons policy.","It shows capacity-building and precaution, not a demonstrated existential-risk crisis choice by Jokowi."],"lenses":["1B.3","1B.9"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Govt lays groundwork for uranium mining, broader atomic aspirations","publisher":"The Jakarta Post","publication_date":"2022-12-19","url":"https://www.thejakartapost.com/indonesia/2022/12/19/govt-lays-groundwork-for-uranium-mining-broader-atomic-aspirations","claim":"Jokowi signed PP No. 52/2022, which requires safety analyses for nuclear-material mining and formal declarations that firms will not work in service of nuclear arms.","locator":"lead paragraph and regulation summary","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reputable independent reporting that quotes the president’s action and summarizes the new regulation’s concrete obligations.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 ruler-adjacent regulatory action.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Jokowi attribution in the article.","contrary_evidence":["This is civilian nuclear-material regulation, not an arms program.","The article is journalistic synthesis of the regulation, not the legal text itself."],"lenses":["1B.3","1B.9","1B.10"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"PP No. 52 Tahun 2022","publisher":"Peraturan BPK / Government of Indonesia","publication_date":"2022-12-12","url":"https://peraturan.bpk.go.id/Details/232967/pp-no-52-tahun-2022","claim":"PP No. 52/2022 regulates safety, security, and management across all stages of nuclear-mineral mining and imposes administrative sanctions for security violations.","locator":"abstract and metadata, lines 20-27 and 118-123","source_type":"primary/legal","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official regulation database with the enacted text summary and promulgation metadata.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Direct 2022 legal change.","ruler_attribution":"Government/regulatory act under Jokowi’s administration; the page itself does not name the signer.","contrary_evidence":["This is regulatory safety law, not evidence of weaponization or nuclear escalation.","It mainly shows civil nuclear governance and enforcement capacity."],"lenses":["1B.3","1B.9"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Menlu RI: Senjata nuklir ancaman nyata bagi umat manusia","publisher":"ANTARA News","publication_date":"2022-09-27","url":"https://www.antaranews.com/berita/3141201/menlu-ri-senjata-nuklir-ancaman-nyata-bagi-umat-manusia","claim":"Indonesia’s foreign minister said nuclear weapons are a real threat to humanity, cited more than 13,000 weapons worldwide, and urged disarmament, stronger global mechanisms, and peaceful nuclear use.","locator":"paras. 69-80","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reputable Indonesian wire report on an official ministerial statement with explicit quotation and timing.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 statement on the anniversary of nuclear disarmament day.","ruler_attribution":"State position via Jokowi’s foreign ministry, not Jokowi personally.","contrary_evidence":["Attribution is to the foreign minister, not the president himself.","It is advocacy, not an operational security decision or treaty act by Jokowi."],"lenses":["1B.1","1B.2","1B.4"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Non-Nuclear-Armed States Get Nothing in Return for Fulfilling Commitments Except Threat of Potential Annihilation, First Committee Told","publisher":"United Nations Press Coverage","publication_date":"2022-10-14","url":"https://press.un.org/en/2022/gadis3690.doc.htm","claim":"Indonesia, speaking for the Non-Aligned Movement and in national capacity, said nuclear-weapon States justify retaining arsenals by citing the security environment, warned against continued possession or threat of use, and urged CTBT, NWFZ, and other disarmament steps.","locator":"Statements section, Indonesia/Mr. Koba","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"UN press coverage of the First Committee session with direct quotation and speaker identification.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 multilateral diplomacy on nuclear disarmament.","ruler_attribution":"Indonesian state position via the UN mission; not a personal Jokowi decision.","contrary_evidence":["This is a multilateral diplomatic posture, not proof of president-level control over nuclear forces.","It reflects a longstanding Indonesian line rather than a new 2022 risk-bearing move."],"lenses":["1B.1","1B.2","1B.4","1B.10"]}

Search and rejection summary
- I considered roughly 30 documents across Setkab presidential transcripts, UNODA treaty pages, IAEA and ASEAN legal databases, BAPETEN and BPK legal pages, ANTARA and The Jakarta Post reporting, and several Reuters-linked items on Ukraine, G20, and nuclear rhetoric.
- I rejected duplicate or redundant items where they repeated the same claim already captured more cleanly, especially the G20 Bali declaration article, later 2023-2026 Kemlu disarmament updates, and multiple pages that restated PP No. 52/2022 without adding a new ruler-attributed fact.
- I rejected out-of-period or low-yield sources such as 2023-2026 disarmament statements when a 2022 source already showed the same Indonesian posture, plus generic defense or economic stories that did not add nuclear/existential-risk evidence.
- I rejected blocked or unhelpful pages, including the JS-gated ASEAN treaty page when the ASEAN legal-instrument table already had the ratification date, and a few UN/press pages that surfaced only as metadata or were inaccessible in-browser.
- I kept sources that do one of three things: establish Jokowi’s actual authority/constraints, document a 2022 Jokowi choice, or confirm Indonesia’s 2022 nuclear nonproliferation and civilian-safety posture.

Remaining gaps
- There is still no evidence of any nuclear command-and-control, arsenal, deployment, or near-use choice by Jokowi in 2022, which is expected because Indonesia is not a nuclear-armed state.
- I found no direct 2022 ruler-level evidence on AI, cyber, or biological catastrophic-risk governance that would materially change Chapter 1B.
- The strongest 2022 ruler-specific nuclear-adjacent act is civilian regulatory: Jokowi signing PP No. 52/2022 on nuclear-mineral safety and security. That is meaningful, but it is not a weapons or crisis-use decision.
- Additional searching would mostly refine attribution around the foreign-ministry and regulator posture, not change the core exposure assessment.
